@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Actual selected-player distance receiver — separate local candidate
+
+Frozen publication candidate f71ec28aa5fb48157429131d8097bf6fbda987ae and its12-file patch/metadata remain unchanged. This follow-up is separate, untested and unpublished; no game, tests, compilation, rendering, CI, merge, uploads or phone/resource changes.
+
+## Existing source input and actual caller
+
+The published player_skills523._apply_numeric_distance_input already supplies exact bound SpellClass.CastRange through a configurable labelled distance-input policy, records the full row's bound SHA, current original archive identity and actual policy-byte SHA, and explicitly says the original distance scale is unconfirmed. It currently skips IsAttackRange=true and MinCastRange!=0. This follow-up does not edit that reader, change a policy value or activate its skipped branches.
+
+New `scripts/skills/current523_distance_receiver.gd::check(world, skill, target, expected={})` is called by SkillService.cast AFTER existing actual target selection/target_allowed and BEFORE spend. An admitted projection gets a runtime-only source_distance_snapshot. The existing SkillService.impact callback rechecks that same snapshot BEFORE its current damage/status/turn-undead branch. No second cost, cooldown, RNG, event, save, source effect or animation stage is added. Missing source distance metadata preserves existing host behavior; present invalid/stale metadata holds that projected cast rather than silently switching input.
+
+The snapshot binds selected local skill ID, exact original SpellClass ID and row SHA, current source identity, actual policy SHA, projected maximum/minimum world length, target instance and life, field instance and combat generation. Positions are remeasured and are not frozen into the token. A reused target life, field switch, source/policy change or out-of-range target cannot use the old projection. Existing active/owned/level/class/weapon/target eligibility remains the service/catalog owner's responsibility. The existing current523_aden_source_active target-admission guard in World._skill_target is preserved; this module does not enable a separate native-map combat path.
+
+## Data-owner input contract
+
+Existing `skill.source523.distance_numeric_input` remains the carrier. Require its original current source identity, spell_id, bound_row_sha256, policy_path, policy_schema, policy_sha256, origin=twilight_adjustable_numeric_estimate, source_raw_distance_unit_scale=unconfirmed, native_grid_scale_recovered=false and host_geometry=existing_host_distance_engine_retained. The receiver reuses PLAYER._source_row_json against the full canonical SpellClass and reads the EXISTING DISTANCE_INPUT_POLICY_PATH; no new source loader/policy/default numeric value is created.
+
+Supported actual target paths are existing active attack/status/turn_undead single/circle/target_circle with target_filter already applied, original TargettingTypeID2 and IsAttackRange=false. Existing range field evidence must be {source_field:CastRange, raw_value:actual original CastRange, multiplier:the existing positive cast_range_to_host_length, host_length_input:that product}, and skill.range must equal it. Its unit is existing world-position Euclidean length (pixels), not a recovered original cell size.
+
+Optional new `distance_numeric_input.fields.min_range` must contain source_field=MinCastRange, the exact original raw_value, the same existing positive multiplier, exact host_length_input product, and explicit comparison=host_center_distance_gte. A positive original MinCastRange without that complete input is blocked. Zero minimum needs no new field. The comparison is an explicit host center-distance receiver contract, not claimed original server boundary behavior. The resulting minimum must be nonnegative, finite and no larger than maximum. The same min/max and existing line-of-sight API are checked against the selected primary target before cost and at impact. Radius/secondary-target/shape semantics stay unchanged.
+
+The current data reader DOES NOT emit positive-minimum inputs; publication of this receiver is not proof of that data-side connection, observed runtime use or approval to change it. Reference-only, Test/dummy, unbound, unsupported weapon-relative and excluded spell-stage/potion/emoticon branches remain unactivated.
+
+## Actual equipped gameplay weapon context
+
+`world.original_skills.current_source_weapon_context()` delegates to `weapon_context(world) -> {ok:true, physical_id,item_class_id,source_id,bless_raw,enchant,weapon_type_id,weapon_type_row,original_item_row,source,source_basis,use_authorized:false}` or {ok:false,reason}. It reads the ACTUAL equipped_items.weapon.instance_id, matching live physical object and current source DTO/full ItemClass/archive, preserves normal/blessed/cursed qualified source IDs through existing original/owned-definition checks, and applies the EXISTING equipment condition helper. Exact ItemBonus→WeaponType is obtained from patch523_ammo.weapon_type(record) and compared with canonical original WeaponType.ID. No Sprite/local_type conversion, legacy-name match, physical identity manufacture, grant or save occurs.
+
+The returned WeaponType.AttackRange is the raw original row used by the existing normal-attack cell consumer. It is NOT automatically a world-length spell range, proof of IsAttackRange meaning, a source scale, or permission to override a skill's existing weapon restriction. This metadata API is available to the data owner for a later exact typed connection; check() continues to reject weapon-relative projection until that separate contract is established.
+
+No asset/raw original table/player receipt/save bytes are included. Public baseline af3ec2b3 and all earlier local commits remain preserved. New publication needs its own exact approval; the pending frozen12-file approval must not include these additional files implicitly.
+
+Read-only caller API: SkillService.source_distance_context(record, actual_target, expected={}) resolves the selected skill through the EXISTING catalog, calls this receiver, and always reports use_authorized=false. It neither spends nor queues an attack. Cast/impact remain the actual execution owners and run their existing readiness/ownership checks.
