@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Existing circular source-area operand receiver — separate local follow-up
+
+Parent checkpoint fe90888ae11c71ab6b5b2ee63a777f750ddce422 and frozen f71ec28aa5fb48157429131d8097bf6fbda987ae publication scopes are preserved unchanged. This additional candidate is not included in either pending approval. Uncompiled, unexecuted, unverified; no game/tests/render/CI/upload/merge/phone/resource changes.
+
+## Original input already supplied
+
+player_skills523._apply_numeric_distance_input already supplies TargetAreaRadius for (TargettingTypeID1, shape self_circle) or (TargettingTypeID2, shape circle/target_circle), using the existing area_radius_to_host_length scale and a labelled unconfirmed-unit numeric policy. It emits distance_numeric_input.fields.radius with full canonical SpellClass-row SHA, current archive identity and actual policy-byte SHA. This follow-up adds no source loader, policy value, unit recovery, new spell or source shape.
+
+## Actual consumer calls
+
+SkillService.cast validates SOURCE_AREA.check after its existing target/landing checks and BEFORE spend/cooldown/effects. An admitted projection carries a runtime-only source_area_snapshot into the same existing queued area/targeted attack. SkillService.impact rechecks the snapshot before its existing effect branch. SkillService.targets also checks the projection/snapshot before running the unchanged actual selector. AUTO's existing self_circle empty-target check therefore uses the same receiver. Read-only API: world.original_skills.source_area_context(record, actual_primary=null, expected={}); it resolves the existing catalog and always returns use_authorized=false.
+
+Snapshot identity includes local skill/original SpellClass ID, bound row/policy SHA, archive, projected radius, existing shape/target cap, actual player/primary instance and primary life, field instance and combat generation. It deliberately does NOT freeze center coordinates or target membership. At use time the existing selector still centers on current player position or current primary position, applies its existing target_allowed and line-of-sight filter, sorts by current distance and uses the same existing target limit. No target, callback, hit, random draw, cost, save or source admission is added by this check.
+
+## Scope and explicit holds
+
+Only existing active attack/status/turn_undead with target_filter applied and the exact matching original self/target circle shape are accepted. Canonical whole-row identity, non-Test/non-excluded source, IsAttackRange=false, MinCastRange0, positive TargetAreaRadius and the complete original radius projection are required. Wrong/missing/stale explicit evidence does not fall back to host radius. Absence of a radius projection preserves existing host behavior. Self circles must not receive a primary; target circles require their actual live primary. Positive MinCastRange is not an inner radius and remains outside this area adapter; weapon-relative area, line/cone/chain/new target roles remain unsupported.
+
+The shared distance receiver's _policy now accepts one of the existing whitelisted scale fields (default cast_range_to_host_length, or area_radius_to_host_length). Existing distance calls keep their original default and behavior. Area does not duplicate the source-policy reader or choose a new conversion number. Source raw units remain unconfirmed and all results report native_area_rule_verified=false.
+
+Input: skill.source523.distance_numeric_input.fields.radius={source_field:TargetAreaRadius,raw_value:exact row.TargetAreaRadius,multiplier:existing policy.area_radius_to_host_length,host_length_input:that exact product}; skill.radius must equal it. Success returns handled:true/ok:true/snapshot/radius_world_length/origin:twilight_adjustable_numeric_estimate/native_area_rule_verified:false. No applicable radius returns handled:false/ok:true. Explicit invalid input returns handled:true/ok:false/reason. This metadata/API is not spell ownership or effect authorization.
+
+All original identity/learning/role/level/weapon/cost/source-target restrictions remain with the existing owner. No NPC identity, Map/Land admission, shape/unit/lifetime rule, positive-minimum formula, image, Sprite, spell-stage, potion or emoticon is fabricated. Sound remains excluded.
